This facility is also a participant in the Occupational Health and Safety 
Administrations (OSHA) Voluntary Protection Program (VPP) to promote effective 
worksite-based safety and health and have qualified for VPP Star status, which is 
recognition for exemplary achievement in the prevention and control of 
occupational safety and health hazards and the development, implementation and 
continuous improvement of safety and health management systems. Approval into 
VPP is OSHAs official recognition of the outstanding efforts of employers and 
employees who have achieved exemplary occupational safety and health.
Five-Year Accident History 
This facility has not had any accidental releases subject to EPA 40 CFR Part 68, within the last five years. 

Emergency Response Program 
In accordance with a June 14, 2018, determination by EPA Region 7, the Seneca Terminal
. is designated as a non-responding facility, and the information specified in Section 9. Emergency Response of the RMP is based on such designation. Notwithstanding, the Seneca Terminal. has an extensive emergency response program with a written Emergency Response Plan (ERP). The ERP is designed as a guide to help in determining the magnitude of an incident, the steps needed to bring the incident under control and the requirements to ensure that all federal, state, and local laws are complied with. The ERP is
